; VISUAL SHOWCASE SECTION
;
; A real, playable ~200m stretch of BREAKLINE built to answer one
; question: does the FRACTURE PROTOCOL visual identity hold up in the
; engine? It runs the same player, spawners, pools, materials and
; destruction as Level01 -- the differences are exactly three:
;   1. ShowcaseDirector places seven gameplay beats by hand
;      (both managers run with auto_spawn = false),
;   2. showcase.tres moves the player at a flat 6 m/s so shards can be
;      read as they approach,
;   3. the track is 200m instead of 900m, with the anomaly count pinned
;      so the magenta accent is guaranteed to appear without becoming
;      wallpaper.
;
; Lighting is intentionally IDENTICAL to Level01 (same environment, same
; single directional light): a showcase lit better than the game would be
; measuring the wrong thing.
;
; The section has no ending -- past the last beat the player keeps moving
; over empty track until they hit the obstacle or quit. That is fine for
; a look-at build and is NOT how the authored level system will work.

